<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Arnotts confirms lower half yr result.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Arnotts confirms lower half yr result.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to January 24, 1997</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   50.77  vs  59.70</p>
<p>    Net				     8.52  vs  38.66</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	 12.0   vs  12.0</p>
<p>    Sales				  343.51 vs 357.42</p>
<p>    Other income			   1.05 vs   2.05</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    6.1  vs  27.8</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			37.13 vs    nil</p>
<p>Dividend is franked at 36 percent</p>
<p>Pay date April 24  </p>
<p>Reg date April 17</p>
<p>    Tax					4.56 vs  20.60</p>
<p>    Interest expense		     0.25 vs   0.53</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  12.86 vs  13.26</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.57 vs   0.44</p>
<p>NOTE: Arnotts Ltd is a biscuit maker, and is majority owned by Campbell Soup Co of the United States. Arnotts released some details of its half year results on February 12.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
